# asahi: Release saved sampler view reference
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46748 state=merged
# ### What does this MR do and why?

While debugging excessive memory usage on my Macbook Pro M1 16GB, I found a memory leak on a sampler view reference:

```
/* asahi_compute_save, line 270 */
pipe_sampler_view_reference(&blitter->saved_sampler_view,
                            &stage->textures[0]->base);          /* +1 on the view */

/* asahi_compute_restore, line 297 */
if (blitter->saved_sampler_view) {
   pctx->set_sampler_views(pctx, MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE, 0, 1, 0,
                           &blitter->saved_sampler_view);       /* slot takes its own +1 */
   blitter->saved_sampler_view = NULL;                          /* save's +1 is never dropped */
}
```

In the discussion in https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45825 I had Claude write memory analysis scripts and a GALLIUM_REFCNT_LOG summarizer. The unbind on or after flush didn't turn out to be the culprit despite helping the problem initially. 

Measurements (M1 Pro, Mesa 26.2.7 release build, darktable-cli, <N> exports of a 4920×3280 raw, medians):

| variant | exports | median runtime | median peak Shmem | median Texture at end |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| without fix | 8 | 39.6 s | +9509 MB | 8397 MB |
| with fix | 16 | 64.2 s | +2895 MB | 496 MB |


If this already classifies as too much AI usage, please ignore the MR.

